{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>If in the break-in.</b> This implies specifically when he came by way of a break-in — that he broke into the house to enter. But if he entered by way of the entrance, he is liable to death, for he is certainly not coming to kill, since he says in his heart: if the homeowner comes to stand against me over his property, he will flee — through the entrance."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:50.338007738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}